\label{def: well fac}
Let $D\geq 1$ be a real number. We say an arithmetic function $\xi:\mathbb{N}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}$ \emph{well-factorable} of level $D$ if, for any choice of factorization $D = D_1D_2$ with $D_1, D_2 \geq 1$, there exist two arithmetic functions $\xi_1, \xi_2:\mathbb{N}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}$ such that
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
\item $|\xi_1|, |\xi_2|\leq 1$.
\item $\xi_1$ is supported on $[1, D_1]$ and $\xi_2$ is supported on $[1, D_2]$.
\item We have\footnote{In general, we do not require the co-primality condition in the definition of $\xi$. However, in order to avoid some technical issues, we impose this condition here.}
\[\xi(d)=\sum_{\substack{d_1d_2=d\\(d_1, d_2)=1}}\xi_1(d_1)\xi_2(d_2).\]
\end{enumerate}

\label{Main Theorem3}
