We note that since $q|X = b^k$ and $(n, b)=1$ (as $\mathfrak{f}(n)$ is supported on integers $n$ such that $(n , b)=1$), the congruence $n\equiv m\imod q$ implies that we either have $(m, q)=1$ or the above sum is empty.
